 him what to do  now that that's a story that I know sits  in people's heads why it has conflict  it's man versus nature the little girl  died you know man versus nature it has  person place and time there's a little  girl it's in Myanmar right  become a master my counsel to you is  become a student of Storytelling  I just gave you a very brief there's  actually a project at Stanford called  this story telling project become a  student of story learn how to tell story  observe people telling story because  story is something so critical to  letting people when you try to  communicate with them to get it in their  head  story is how it gets there  and that's why I said go watch Netflix  or Hulu or whatever tonight you will see  the three one of the three examples in  everything you watch  and it is always conflict just to be  clear it is always conflict when people  do reference calls which Once Upon a  Time people did a lot of the question is  never oh you know why did you buy this  or are you happy that's all kind of like  obviously the reference is not going to  be a reference I said the question they  will always ask is what stood in your  way how did you convince your boss to do  this what was the conflict you had to  resolve the conflict is what is in our  heads what buries in our heads and I  will tell you get good at this learn  about storytelling because it's a  powerful way of communication  which leads me to  the power of language  so I used to do the first uh first line  manager education at Oracle I used to do  the one of the lectures talk about uh  management and I said to these young  managers I said well you know most of  you are thinking that as a manager what  you want is to have more people working  for you right that's kind of the goal  I'm going to have more and more and more  people  and I said yeah that's fine there  certainly are challenges in having more  and more people  but at the end of the day the big  challenge is not about owning more  people it's about owning more Minds  when you own the mind you own the people  and this is really really true when you  become more and more senior in  management is you're not sitting there  you know trying to dictate what one  person does for from eight to five or  whatever what you're trying to do is get  your team get your group get these  people to head in a particular direction  right now how do you own mind  the only way to own mind is to own  language language is how we think how we  communicate  and so I always say to people well you  know if you want to go be a successful  startup in France you better go learn  French right  I mean it the language is is  horrendously important and people I  think oftentimes are very lacks about  how they use language Let me give you an  example  um  I told you at the very beginning I  started up the cloud computing business  at Oracle one of the things that we  faced in the applications was because  these applications were never engineered  to be delivered in a consistent way  there was often times people would say  well  we we can't use it out of the box we  have to customize it  and over time Larry who's still the CEO  at Oracle would say Donna please don't  change our software don't customize it  so then the field the field sales guys  the field Engineers would go oh well  we're not really customizing we're  configuring right uh you know because  customization's bad so we're configuring  uh no we're not really configuring we're  extending it right  and after a while I kept hearing all  this coming out of the fields going what  the hell are you guys talking about what  what does this mean  and so I got one of the engineering vice  presidents I said okay I want you to  list me all the different reasons why  someone might have to change the  software that was shipped  whether as simple as adding a report  or as complex as adding a trigger  he came up with 26 different classes  uh I took all the words I usually hate  acronyms but I took all the words I had  heard customization extension  modification  localizations Integrations and I put  them all together in one word in fact  for a little while it was on Wikipedia  it was  c-e-m-l-i was the acronym  and we actually taught people how to  pronounce this word right it was  pronounced chemli  and and so we kept using the word  explaining to people what the word was  what was fascinating was within less  than a year you could figure out in the  very first conversation whether that  team was part of our tribe or not  because they either exactly knew what  the word meant or they were looking at  you going what are you talking about  and over a longer term the whole  Consulting organization actually adopted  the framework and adopted the word I'm  using that as a simple example of owning  language and owning a word as an example  of owning what people think about and  how they think  and so as you go and you know work in  some company or start your own  how you communicate and remember I made  the comment about Sid and you know the  written word it's another example of  this the words you choose the language  you choose  that is extremely powerful and make them  make the choice of that language don't  be sloppy about the language because if  you are then you cannot communicate with  people if one day you're saying uh you  know I'm calling it a edge server in the  next day an edge cloud and the next day  an edge computer you're you know what  did you mean so the consistency of  language your choice of that language  very powerful in making sure you're  communicating and you're I'm going to  say it owning people's minds  lesson five  manage your career  so as you know I keep like tell stories  so I'll tell you another story  this is a guy I went to graduate school  many years ago  he calls me up one day and we haven't  talked in probably 20 years  and he said you know I uh I just got  laid off  um really liked some advice so I said  cool so we